Hadoop WordCount - Steps

1) Start Hadoop Services

start-dfs.sh && start-yarn.sh

2) Create Folder in HDFS

hdfs dfs-mkdir /cloud

hdis dfs -ls/

hdfs dfs -mkdir /wordcount

hdfs dfs -mkdir /cloud/input

hdfs dfs -mkdir /cloud/output

3) Create Text File for Input

touch wordinput.

nano wordinput

4) Push File to HDFS

hdfs dfs-put wordinput/wordcount/input

5) Go to Eclipse

Create Java Project (name: wordcount, JRE: Java 8)

Create class: main.java

Add Hadoop JARS:

hadoop-client-core-3.2.1.jar

hadoop-common-3.2.1.jar

Import required libraries

6) Export JAR

Right click project Export JAR file

7) Run Hadoop Job

hadoop jar wordcount.jar wordcount /wordcount/input/wordinput/wordcount/output

8) View Output

hdfs dfs-cat/wordcount/output/part-r-00000

